WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.208 --> 00:00:06.646
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:15.388 --> 00:00:18.691
I remember in some job interviews
I had during grad school,

00:00:18.691 --> 00:00:22.695
they would sometimes ask me where
do I see myself in five years.

00:00:22.695 --> 00:00:24.831
I never knew how to
answer that question.

00:00:24.831 --> 00:00:27.867
And now, that I'm lost
inside a drainage pipe

00:00:27.867 --> 00:00:30.736
in a chemical processing
plant, this is why.

00:00:30.736 --> 00:00:32.471
Oh, this looks promising.

00:00:32.471 --> 00:00:34.807
I was expecting spinning saw blades.

00:00:34.807 --> 00:00:35.975
Or a pool of acid.

00:00:35.975 --> 00:00:37.109
This is much better.

00:00:38.511 --> 00:00:40.346
But, why are there no doors here?

00:00:40.346 --> 00:00:43.549
Did I actually enter this
room in the correct manner?

00:00:43.549 --> 00:00:45.451
Maybe the room itself is alive.

00:00:45.451 --> 00:00:46.452
Um...

00:00:46.452 --> 00:00:47.753
OH MY GOD!  I'M GONNA D--

00:00:47.753 --> 00:00:50.923
[underwater mumbling]

00:00:51.524 --> 00:00:53.392
Okay!  I'm awake!

00:00:53.392 --> 00:00:55.294
I was a little drowsy, now I'm awake.

00:00:55.294 --> 00:00:57.697
Oh!  Yuck!  What is--

00:00:57.697 --> 00:00:59.565
That-- that is nasty!

00:00:59.565 --> 00:01:01.601
I do not have to accept this.

00:01:01.601 --> 00:01:02.235
[lock jiggles]

00:01:02.235 --> 00:01:03.603
Oh, you bastards.

00:01:04.337 --> 00:01:04.971
Fine...

00:01:05.571 --> 00:01:07.773
Got to avoid the blood shower...

00:01:07.773 --> 00:01:10.042
This isn't the sort of thing
I should have to worry about.

00:01:10.042 --> 00:01:12.311
Jesus!  Where's this coming from?

00:01:12.311 --> 00:01:13.846
Maybe we don't even ship in meat.

00:01:13.846 --> 00:01:16.249
We just slaughter the cows
right here at the facility.

00:01:16.249 --> 00:01:19.085
And then just dump them in the water
like we know what we're doing.

00:01:19.085 --> 00:01:22.088
Oh my god! This better
not get in my hair.

00:01:22.088 --> 00:01:25.324
If I wanted to smell like McDonald's,
I would've stayed in the trash compactor.

00:01:25.324 --> 00:01:26.225
[lock jiggles]

00:01:26.225 --> 00:01:27.693
No! Open up!

00:01:27.693 --> 00:01:29.762
FBI! I have a warrant!

00:01:30.463 --> 00:01:32.965
Hey!  Hello!

00:01:33.599 --> 00:01:34.934
[growls]

00:01:34.934 --> 00:01:37.303
I shouldn't be surprised
the doors are locked.

00:01:37.303 --> 00:01:40.106
No one likes to hang out
in the meat dumping room.

00:01:40.106 --> 00:01:41.307
Not even on break.

00:01:41.307 --> 00:01:42.842
So, how am I getting out of here?

00:01:42.842 --> 00:01:44.644
I'm not swimming through the fan blades.

00:01:44.644 --> 00:01:46.579
That's an easy option to scratch off.

00:01:46.579 --> 00:01:50.583
And I somehow don't see myself
shimmying up a sheet metal wall.

00:01:50.583 --> 00:01:52.718
I am definitely late for work.

00:01:52.718 --> 00:01:53.486
Oh well!

00:01:53.486 --> 00:01:54.487
Guess I'll go with the flow!

00:01:56.155 --> 00:02:01.794
[underwater mumbling]

00:02:01.794 --> 00:02:05.731
Fuck, I just know some of these
meat chunks are getting in my hair.

00:02:05.731 --> 00:02:08.467
I'm going to need some
serious shampoo after this.

00:02:08.467 --> 00:02:11.437
I'm not a leper. I shouldn't have to
stand for meat dandruff.

00:02:12.538 --> 00:02:14.440
The exit must be on the other side.

00:02:15.808 --> 00:02:18.978
[underwater mumbling]

00:02:18.978 --> 00:02:22.081
I wonder how fast I'd have to run
to skip on top of the water.

00:02:22.081 --> 00:02:23.716
It smells funny here.

00:02:23.716 --> 00:02:25.918
And, there is no exit.

00:02:25.918 --> 00:02:27.453
What the hell, people?

00:02:27.453 --> 00:02:28.220
What's this?

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:29.522
Ah, more water.

00:02:30.256 --> 00:02:30.823
Oh.

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:33.326
That would explain the smell.

00:02:33.326 --> 00:02:35.061
What the hell are we spraying?

00:02:35.061 --> 00:02:36.228
I don't like orange.

00:02:36.228 --> 00:02:38.931
Orange is a bad color
for industrial chemicals.

00:02:38.931 --> 00:02:41.334
We could get away with this
if we were making Cheetos.

00:02:41.334 --> 00:02:45.104
But I'm 80% sure
Cheetos aren't made like this.

00:02:45.104 --> 00:02:47.740
Hm, looks like I need to keep on swimming.

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:48.541
Can opener!

00:02:49.375 --> 00:02:57.249
[underwater mumbling]

00:02:58.017 --> 00:03:00.753
Yeah, swimming upstream is for losers.

00:03:00.753 --> 00:03:02.521
Losers and salmon.

00:03:02.521 --> 00:03:03.489
Cool ceiling.

00:03:03.489 --> 00:03:04.290
[underwater mumbling]

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:06.659
[gagging, choking]

00:03:06.659 --> 00:03:08.361
Uncool undertoe!

00:03:09.061 --> 00:03:11.430
Aaaahhhh....

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:13.532
This is a pretty shitty water park.

00:03:13.532 --> 00:03:15.234
I'm not coming here again.

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:16.736
Oh, god, there's that gas.

00:03:16.736 --> 00:03:18.237
I don't want to breathe this!

00:03:18.738 --> 00:03:19.638
[inhale]

00:03:21.207 --> 00:03:34.320
[underwater mumbling]

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:35.821
[gasping]

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:40.259
Jesus!  Gas and a rotating crusher!

00:03:40.259 --> 00:03:42.728
Maybe I shouldn't be going this way.

00:03:42.728 --> 00:03:46.032
Well, hey! This room looks like something!

00:03:46.032 --> 00:03:48.067
It has steps and everything.

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:50.936
That means I'm done with
the meat processing ride!

00:03:50.936 --> 00:03:54.040
I think my values have dropped
considerably since I woke up.

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:58.277
Instead of getting to work on
time, now I just want not die.

00:03:58.277 --> 00:04:02.415
And... oh, my god.
This is that same room.

00:04:02.415 --> 00:04:04.850
I've gone in a giant circle again.

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:06.185
This is horrible!

00:04:06.185 --> 00:04:10.956
Well, I suppose this good preparation
for later in life if I get Alzheimer's.

00:04:10.956 --> 00:04:12.625
I'll wake up not remembering everything

00:04:12.625 --> 00:04:14.894
but still be able to escape
the retirement home.

00:04:14.894 --> 00:04:15.928
Wait, what am I saying?

00:04:15.928 --> 00:04:17.530
I'm not going to get Alzheimer's.

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:20.433
People who stay mentally active
have resistance against that.

00:04:20.433 --> 00:04:22.468
And I mentally dominate everyone!

00:04:22.468 --> 00:04:25.337
When I get old, I'm going to
buy that walking cane I saw

00:04:25.337 --> 00:04:27.339
that secretly transforms into a sword

00:04:27.339 --> 00:04:30.643
and scare the hell out anyone
who doesn't show me respect.

00:04:31.777 --> 00:04:40.152
[underwater mumbling]

00:04:41.554 --> 00:04:44.890
Glad to see air is part of
today's itinerary.

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:48.294
Hm, I wonder if I'll need a
separate shampoo for my beard

00:04:48.294 --> 00:04:49.462
than I will for my hair.

00:04:49.462 --> 00:04:51.530
Oh, another gun.

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:52.598
Whah!

00:04:52.998 --> 00:04:55.801
Okay, what the fuck did I just shoot?

00:04:55.801 --> 00:04:58.637
I'm totally justified, whatever it is.

00:04:58.637 --> 00:05:02.842
Looks like a cross between
a leopard and...  Cthulhu.

00:05:02.842 --> 00:05:05.945
Yep. That's definitely not a cockroach.

00:05:05.945 --> 00:05:08.881
Wait, I've seen these things before.

00:05:08.881 --> 00:05:12.084
Oh, shit! I remember now!

00:05:12.084 --> 00:05:13.919
These are aliens!

00:05:13.919 --> 00:05:17.490
Of course. I remember everything.

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:19.325
I was in the test chamber.

00:05:19.325 --> 00:05:21.427
I was going to load the new sample in.

00:05:21.427 --> 00:05:23.562
Then, somebody cut the lights.

00:05:23.562 --> 00:05:26.398
And then some of the scientists
put on these creepy-looking robes

00:05:26.398 --> 00:05:28.167
and started lighting torches.

00:05:28.167 --> 00:05:29.802
Then one of them got on the intercom

00:05:29.802 --> 00:05:32.138
and starting chanting this crazy ritual.

00:05:32.138 --> 00:05:35.741
Next thing I know, we have beings from
another dimension teleporting in here

00:05:35.741 --> 00:05:37.676
like we're giving away free t-shirts.

00:05:38.677 --> 00:05:41.280
Oh no! Not this room again!

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:43.549
I don't understand!

00:05:43.549 --> 00:05:45.985
Why do we make rooms
that can't be accessed

00:05:45.985 --> 00:05:49.288
connect to other rooms
that can't be accessed?

00:05:49.288 --> 00:05:51.590
I bet this guy died trying to get out.

00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:52.791
Hey, what's this?

00:05:52.791 --> 00:05:55.394
Oh! Satchel charges!

00:05:55.394 --> 00:05:59.064
These are how you create your own exits!

00:05:59.064 --> 00:06:01.333
Glad they were just lying on this desk.

00:06:01.333 --> 00:06:04.303
Wow, these things have a
remote control and everything.

00:06:04.303 --> 00:06:05.604
Maybe I should hold onto these.

00:06:05.604 --> 00:06:07.673
I bet I could sell them for a good price.

00:06:07.706 --> 00:06:10.042
I'm sure Eddie would take these
off my hands for me.

00:06:10.042 --> 00:06:11.343
He loves this stuff.

00:06:11.343 --> 00:06:13.879
This could turn out to be
a good day after all.

00:06:13.879 --> 00:06:16.048
I think the revolver must be a Magnum.

00:06:16.048 --> 00:06:18.517
That thing felt like I was God!

00:06:18.517 --> 00:06:19.852
Pew!

00:06:19.852 --> 00:06:22.655
Thou shalt not eat my face!

00:06:22.655 --> 00:06:24.557
I am the Lord thy God!

00:06:24.557 --> 00:06:26.859
Behold me push these switches!

00:06:28.694 --> 00:06:30.796
Hey, these aren't doing anything.

00:06:30.796 --> 00:06:33.365
There. Now they're all
in the "Off" position.

00:06:33.365 --> 00:06:34.533
Piece of crap.

00:06:34.533 --> 00:06:38.404
Why make a switch box that's
clearly labeled, easily accessible,

00:06:38.404 --> 00:06:40.306
if it doesn't actually work?

00:06:40.306 --> 00:06:43.309
Now, an optimist would say,
"Hey, that's two out of three."

00:06:43.309 --> 00:06:44.843
I say, "That's bullshit!"

00:06:45.644 --> 00:06:48.747
Ugh! I wasn't asking
for a second opinion!

00:06:49.582 --> 00:06:50.916
Least of all yours!

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:53.986
This is NOT a democracy!

00:06:53.986 --> 00:06:56.789
I have a gun so I'm in charge!

00:06:56.789 --> 00:06:59.925
Many governments around the world
function on this principle!

00:06:59.925 --> 00:07:01.560
And some of them last for months!

00:07:03.395 --> 00:07:05.497
This is not complicated!

00:07:05.497 --> 00:07:07.266
You're making it that way!

00:07:07.266 --> 00:07:08.200
BLAH!

00:07:10.402 --> 00:07:14.206
Well, I guess the good news is:
I'm not late for work like I thought.

00:07:14.206 --> 00:07:16.742
No work today. We have too many problems.

00:07:16.742 --> 00:07:17.810
Like, death.

00:07:18.344 --> 00:07:21.914
That was a pretty big problem
for a lot of the faculty if I recall.

00:07:21.914 --> 00:07:24.216
I mean, it wasn't for me, but, c'mon.

00:07:24.216 --> 00:07:27.386
Although maybe I shouldn't be so cocky
about my situation since

00:07:27.386 --> 00:07:31.657
I don't know how to get out of here and
I don't feel like swimming again.

00:07:31.657 --> 00:07:34.693
Although saying that implies
I felt like doing it to begin with.

00:07:34.693 --> 00:07:35.027
Button!

00:07:35.027 --> 00:07:36.028
[rumbling]

00:07:36.028 --> 00:07:36.795
What did that do?

00:07:37.763 --> 00:07:41.133
Ah! Don't mash my potatoes.

00:07:41.133 --> 00:07:45.404
Stop...no...not qui...
yeah, there we go.

00:07:45.404 --> 00:07:48.340
I get it. Turn off the hammers
then the switches.

00:07:48.340 --> 00:07:50.409
It's like sawing
through a body at the joint

00:07:50.409 --> 00:07:52.278
so you don't have to
cut through the bone.

00:07:52.778 --> 00:07:54.780
Wait, it's nothing like that.

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:56.248
I'm confused.

00:07:56.248 --> 00:08:00.185
Okay, I think if I just break everything
life will get simpler.

00:08:00.185 --> 00:08:01.954
Switch one, switch two,

00:08:01.954 --> 00:08:03.722
switch three, you suck.

00:08:03.722 --> 00:08:06.458
And that appears to have done nothing.

00:08:06.458 --> 00:08:10.329
Okay, this is why I
study THEORETICAL physics.

00:08:10.329 --> 00:08:13.065
I don't normally have
to do all the dirty work.

00:08:13.065 --> 00:08:17.303
It is so much easier yelling at a
lab assistant to do things for you.

00:08:17.303 --> 00:08:19.104
Rrr, Jesus Christ.

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:22.374
Body low...

00:08:22.374 --> 00:08:23.709
Whoa-ho!

00:08:23.709 --> 00:08:25.377
Nice speed!

00:08:25.377 --> 00:08:27.479
I guess today's more
interesting than usual.

00:08:27.479 --> 00:08:30.616
I mean I'm bodysurfing on a conveyor
belt at some creepy factory.

00:08:30.649 --> 00:08:31.984
Most people don't do that.

00:08:31.984 --> 00:08:33.218
Even on weekends.

00:08:33.218 --> 00:08:35.454
I hope this leads to one of
those big plastic ball pits

00:08:35.454 --> 00:08:37.189
they have at themed pizza restaurants.

00:08:37.189 --> 00:08:39.692
That would almost make up for
all the switches.

00:08:39.692 --> 00:08:41.393
Ah, no. We're getting off here.

00:08:41.393 --> 00:08:42.361
This part looks good.

00:08:43.796 --> 00:08:44.997
I mean, there's a ladder here.

00:08:44.997 --> 00:08:47.066
Surely, someone was
meant to come this way.

00:08:47.066 --> 00:08:48.467
No.

00:08:48.467 --> 00:08:50.235
No one's ever been here.

00:08:50.235 --> 00:08:51.937
[yawns]

00:08:51.937 --> 00:08:54.606
You know what?
I'm going to go back to sleep.

00:08:54.606 --> 00:08:56.208
It's not like I have to work today.

00:08:56.208 --> 00:08:58.544
[yawns]

00:08:58.544 --> 00:09:00.045
Nom-nom-nom...

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:05.084
Holy shit!

00:09:05.084 --> 00:09:06.085
Was that a bat?

00:09:08.387 --> 00:09:08.921
No?

00:09:10.989 --> 00:09:12.167
Guess not.

